# Traffic Control System (Assembly Language)

A four-way traffic light controller written in assembly language for the
8051 microcontroller. It cycles through green, yellow, and red phases for two
roads (North-South and East-West) with timed delays, so that conflicting
directions never get green at the same time.

## Features
- Two-road intersection (North-South and East-West)
- Green, yellow, and red phases with fixed timing
- Safe sequencing: one road is always red while the other is green or yellow
- Delay routines built on hardware Timer 0
- [Optional: pedestrian button, 7-segment countdown]

## Hardware / Simulator
- 8051 microcontroller (AT89C51)
- 6 LEDs (red, yellow, green for each road) on Port 1
- Simulated in [Keil uVision / EdSim51 / Proteus]

## Pin Map (Port 1)
| Pin  | Signal            |
|------|-------------------|
| P1.0 | NS Red            |
| P1.1 | NS Yellow         |
| P1.2 | NS Green          |
| P1.3 | EW Red            |
| P1.4 | EW Yellow         |
| P1.5 | EW Green          |
